# fixedbugs, defect 2364, lane p239-land-a, 2026-11-09 (panel 239's R4, route
# C; the briefs' `prefix`).
#
# Module `rs_configured` reads `fixedbugs-2364-cfg.h`, which defines the
# macro, before `fixedbugs-2364-rs.h`, so it reads `Rs` wide and binds `a:
# i64`. This module spells `Rs` and has no group of its own, so its unit read
# `rs.h` alone, narrow, and the build was refused, *`Rs.a` is `int`*. Now the
# owner's earlier header is read before the record's here too, and the
# program prints 6.
use fixedbugs2364/rs_configured

function main()
    r = rs_configured.make(v: 3)
    print(r.a + to_i64(r.b).must())
